<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Carians</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Carians were the native people of Caria in south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asia-minor">Asia Minor</a>, speaking an Anatolian language related to Luwian and written in their own alphabet. Greek writers described them as early inhabitants of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aegean">Aegean</a> coasts and islands, and they served widely as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mercenary">mercenaries</a>, including in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>. Under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hecatomnid-dynasty">Hecatomnid dynasty</a>, notably <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mausolus">Mausolus</a> in the fourth century BCE, Caria flourished under Persian rule.</p></div>
